  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 213 AM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nThe main period of interest this forecast period will be this \nevening into Sunday morning as it will provide the only period of \nprecipitation the next 7 days. It will also bring a return to cooler \ntemperatures near to slightly below normal next week. These changes \nwill come courtesy of a cold front that early this morning is \nextending from northeastern Nebraska into western Kansas. Today, a \nupper level trough will move from the eastern Rockies into the \nPlains. This will force the attendant cold front into the area this \nevening. However, out ahead of this front continued WAA will provide \none last warm day with highs in the mid 60s to mid 70s. Showers with \na few thunderstorms are expected to overspread the area tonight \nthrough the overnight as a the cold front moves through the region. \nLight showers are expected to linger through the morning as the \nupper level trough traverses through the region. Strong CAA is \nexpected behind the front tonight into tomorrow morning which will \nusher in much cooler temperatures for Sunday with highs in the mid \n40s to mid 50s. Winds will diminish Sunday night as a surface ridge \nof high pressure builds into are from the northern Plains. Light \nwinds and clear skies Sunday night will usher sub-freezing lows back \ninto the area in the mid 20s to near 30.\n\nMonday through Tuesday, the surface ridge will continue to dominate \nlocal weather providing tranquil but cool conditions as weak mixing \nwill hold highs generally in the 40s. Tuesday night into Wednesday, \na upper level trough will dig through the region with a closed low \nin the base of the trough passing south of the forecast area. This \nwill keep precipitable weather south of area as well but with also \nkeep local temperatures cool with highs remaining in the 40s. \nAnother surface ridge of high pressure will traverse the area \nThursday for the Thanksgiving Day holiday keeping conditions dry \nwith seasonable temperatures with highs in the mid 40s to lower 50s. \nThanksgiving night the surface ridge will slide east of the area with \na brief return to WAA on Friday aiding in highs rising into the mid \n40s to mid 50s.",
